<title>USA: Cryomedical's AccuProbe gets FDA nod.</title>
<headline>Cryomedical's AccuProbe gets FDA nod.</headline>
<dateline>ROCKVILLE, Md. 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cryomedical Sciences Inc said on Wednesday it received 510(k) market clearance from the U.S. Food and Drug Administration for its AccuProbe 600 product.</p>
<p>The AccuProbe 600 series of instruments is less costly to manufacture than its predecessors, the company said. The instruments are used to excise unwanted tissue in minimally invasive surgical procedures.</p>
<p>Cryomedical shares were trading up 3/32 to 15/32 at midday Wednesday.</p>
</text>
